# Factoidal local test override
# See tests/local-overrides/README.md for the convention + runner contract.
suite: graph-store-protocol
test: Graph creation via POST on the GSP endpoint, then GET of the resulting graph (direct graph identification)
category: GraphStoreProtocolTest
upstream-result: POST to the endpoint with no graph parameter creates a new graph, answers 201 Created with a Location header, and GET of the Location IRI returns the graph
our-result: request 1 of 2 fails: SPARQL_GraphStore has no graph creation (no fresh graph IRI, no Location)
kind: engine-gap
disposition: local-override
date: 2026-10-10
issue: https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/698
provenance: w3c/rdf-tests ec2ba15, sparql/sparql11/graph-store-protocol/ (manifest-direct.ttl, manifest-indirect.ttl; structured ht:Connection form from 02f98ff)
---
EXPECTED FAILURE, NOT A DISAGREEMENT WITH THE FIXTURE. The fixture is
correct; the F* tree does not yet provide graph creation by POST with a Location header.

Specification
  GSP section 5.5 (HTTP POST) and section 4: a POST to the Graph Store itself creates a graph in the store; the response is 201 Created and the Location header names the new graph.

What the F* tree has
  SPARQL.GraphStore.fst is a pure store model: gsp_get, gsp_head,
  gsp_put, gsp_post, gsp_delete and the status functions. The runner
  (bin/w3c-runner/w3c_runner.ml, _gsp_run_exchanges) replays the
  structured exchanges over it and parses and compares RDF bodies with the
  F* Turtle parser and RDF.GraphIsomorphism. It has no multipart parser and
  no way to mint the IRI of a created graph, and iron rule 7 forbids adding
  either to the runner. The Lean tree passes this test
  (formal/lean4/L4Factoidal/SPARQL/GraphStoreService.lean).

How this file behaves
  The runner still runs the test. While it fails, it is counted as a
  local-override, apart from pass and fail. When the F* module gains the
  feature and the test passes, the runner marks this override STALE and
  exits non-zero until this file is removed (CLAUDE.md, "A stated
  shortfall is a failing test plus an open issue").

Issue
  The placeholder URL above stands for the issue that tracks "SPARQL.GraphStore
  service: multipart/form-data bodies and graph creation with Location in F*".
